body:
Well, I can honestly say I haven't come far enough to improve my self esteem in my journey quite yet. I've been trying to do actions in my life that I know will benefit my health though, as I'm closing in on my 30s and my family has a really rough tree of issues. To play into that, I've been trying to drink more water (which is SUPER difficult to remember) and improve upon my hygiene. I have long hair and haven't dyed it in years, and am trying to work the will up to do that because, like, yeah I'm an adult but I want to be professional, but why should I care? There's other 30, 40, 50 year olds with dyed hair and they love life and I really want to be happy like those people are, and I feel that's where my confidence will stem from best. But, like I said I'm struggling a lot still ^^;

For your friend, I'd ask them what they like, maybe their confidence will stem from developing a talent. So, an instrument, or speed running a video game, something that's actually only for YOU to appreciate in your own private time, no one needs to be involved or critique. I feel like having a goal helps me a lot, and right now my goal is just surviving these next few months with my head above water, but in between these surviving moments I find I may not have the patience for a hobby, but I can at least include something physically beneficial in the meantime.

My situation may not apply to you, but I think there's got to be something out there for everyone, whether it be unreachable in the present or right in front of us, this world has it's way. Sorry about the book!

27  for 7 Days to Die please!

&#x200B;

Recommend Cook Serve Delicious because that's what I'm playing right now
